# Project Guidelines & Architecture

## Core Tech Stack

* **Framework:** Astro (`.astro` files)
* **Language:** TypeScript (Use standard TS types/interfaces in frontmatter)
* **Styling:** Tailwind CSS

## Design System & Styling Rules

* **Tailwind Configuration:** `tailwind.config.mjs` is the single source of truth for theme tokens (colors, fonts, container max-width). Read that file whenever choosing or applying theme values. Extend new tokens there under `theme.extend` — do not redefine them in this rules file.
* **Strict Color Usage:** Apply theme colors only via the custom Tailwind classes defined in `tailwind.config.mjs`. Do **not** invent arbitrary hex codes or use default Tailwind colors.
* **Typography:** Use `font-sans` / `font-heading` from `tailwind.config.mjs`. Font files live in `/public/fonts/` and are loaded in `src/styles/global.css`.
* **Units:** Do not use `px` for font sizes — use `rem` instead. When the user specifies a value in `px`, always convert it to `rem` first (16px = 1rem) before applying it in code. **Exception:** border radius and border width values may use `px`.
* **Container:** Use the container / `max-w-container` values from `tailwind.config.mjs` (1440px / 90rem). Do not invent a different content max-width.

## Assets

* All image assets are hosted at https://pub-7201b9d69f714980aff6db704be9de2d.r2.dev. Import `asset()` from `src/lib/assets.ts` to build image URLs. Do not hardcode the CDN base in components.

## Responsive & Mobile-First Design

* **Desktop-First Approach:** Write styles for desktop screens by default, then layer on layout and style changes using Tailwind's breakpoint prefixes (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`).
* **Fluid Layouts:** Every component and page layout **must be responsive out of the box**. Do not build desktop-only layouts that overflow on smaller viewports.

## Component Architecture

* **File Structure:** Place all reusable `.astro` components in `src/components/`, page layouts in `src/layouts/`, and pages in `src/pages/`.
* **Islands Architecture:** Keep server-first rendering by default. Only use interactive client directives (`client:load`, `client:idle`, `client:visible`) when strictly necessary for JavaScript interactivity.

### What MUST Be a Component

* **Global Layout Elements:** Navigation bars, footers, and SEO/Head wrappers used across multiple pages.
* **Design System Atoms:** Standardized UI elements that repeat with different data or variants (e.g., `Button.astro`, `InputField.astro`, `Badge.astro`).
* **Data-Driven Repeatable Blocks:** UI structures that map over data or content arrays (e.g., `FeatureCard.astro`, `TestimonialCard.astro`, `PricingCard.astro`).
* **Interactive Islands:** Any client-side dynamic widgets requiring Astro hydration directives like `client:load` or `client:visible` (e.g., mobile menu toggles, accordions, sliders).

### What MUST NOT Be a Component

* **Native Typography:** Do NOT abstract basic HTML text tags into custom components (e.g., do not create `<Heading1>` or `<TextParagraph>`). Apply Tailwind utility classes directly to native `<h1>`–`<h6>` and `<p>` tags.
* **One-Off Page Sections:** Unique layout sections (e.g., a specific Hero section, a specific "About Our Story" layout) must be written directly inside the respective page file (`index.astro`, `about.astro`) instead of being isolated into separate files.
* **Basic Layout Wrappers:** Do not create custom components that just serve as standard CSS wrappers (e.g., replacing `<div class="max-w-container mx-auto px-4">` with a `<Container>` component). Use inline Tailwind classes instead.

### Implementation Code Style

* **Props Typing:** Always define explicit TypeScript interfaces for Astro component props (`interface Props { ... }`).
* **Tailwind Variants:** For components with multiple styles (like Primary vs Secondary buttons), use a clean JavaScript object map or template literal configuration inside the Astro component script frontmatter rather than long, messy inline ternary operations.

## Localization

* **Locales:** Hungarian (`hu`) is the default/primary language. Provide an English (`en`) version of all user-facing copy.
* **Sanity:** Configure Studio and content schemas for both `hu` and `en` (localized fields / documents).
* **Editable vs hardcoded:** Marketing/page content editors should change in Sanity (localized). Structural/chrome UI copy that should stay code-owned stays hardcoded — in both languages in the codebase. When unclear, ask which texts are Sanity-editable vs hardcoded.

## Sanity CMS Editability

* **Sanity-editable content:** Page section copy (headlines, body, CTAs, labels), images (including alt text), and reorderable section blocks — all localized `hu`/`en` where applicable.
* **Hardcoded content:** Skip Sanity for chrome and other code-owned UI (e.g. main navigation labels when kept in code). Hardcode both language variants in the codebase.
* **Section reordering:** Page sections must be modeled so editors can reorder them in Sanity (e.g. an ordered array of section blocks).

## JavaScript Organization & Formatting

* **Modular Files:** Do **not** write monolithic `<script>` tags or massive single JS/TS files. Split logic into small, modular files organized logically in `src/scripts/` or alongside the component.
* **Header Comment Required:** Every JS/TS file **must** start with a brief 1–2 line comment explaining its core purpose. Don't add comments to other file types.

